{
  "comment": [
    "Every runtime GLB the web game loads that came out of the AI Toolkit, and",
    "the numbers needed to turn the generator's output into it.",
    "",
    "sourceFolder is a directory under Assets/Art/Generated in the art drop; it",
    "always holds one selected.fbx plus a selected.fbm texture pair. targetSize",
    "is the longest dimension in metres — the generator's own scale is",
    "arbitrary, so this is where an asset's real size is decided. material is",
    "the stable name the runtime calibration in src/game/08b-generated-art.js",
    "matches on; renaming one here without renaming it there leaves the surface",
    "uncalibrated, and nothing fails to tell you so.",
    "",
    "textureSize is enforced by re-saving the scaled image — see the note on",
    "load_downsampled in convert_generated_fbx.py. It was silently ignored once,",
    "and every asset shipped 2048 maps regardless of what was asked for here.",
    "",
    "rotate is stated rather than inferred because the generator is not",
    "consistent about up/forward, and a wrong guess only shows up in a render.",
    "docs/renders/generated/ holds the proof for each entry.",
    "",
    "Regenerate with: npm run art:convert (from source/)."
  ],
